(4542128, 643912, 75034, '<td valign="top">This reminds me of someone else''s work but I can''t quite put my finger on it, it''s right on the tip of my tongue. Can you see it? Oh I know Leroy. Now we know that this is not his but I glad to see that someone (Jamie?) is carrying on for him with the "in her jeans" theme.<br/> <br/>I was trying to get someone for a shot to honor Leroy but alas I could not and so I''m very pleased to see that you were able to.<br/> <br/>The shot itself is lovely and Christina is beautiful, I love the colour of her tattoos and the background bokeh. I do like the directional sun light but if I may I would of liked to see her looking back over her shoulder. Your pose position is not wrong on any way it''s just how I see it in my mind.<br/> <br/>I think that if you''re getting lessons from Leroy you are a quick study and that he is a good teacher. Keep up the great work and I hope you do well with this and any other challenges you enter.<br/> <br/>All the best <br/> <br/>MAX!</td>', 'This reminds me of someone else''s work but I can''t quite put my finger on it, it''s right on the tip of my tongue. Can you see it? Oh I know Leroy. Now we know that this is not his but I glad to see that someone (Jamie?) is carrying on for him with the "in her jeans" theme. I was trying to get someone for a shot to honor Leroy but alas I could not and so I''m very pleased to see that you were able to. The shot itself is lovely and Christina is beautiful, I love the colour of her tattoos and the background bokeh. I do like the directional sun light but if I may I would of liked to see her looking back over her shoulder. Your pose position is not wrong on any way it''s just how I see it in my mind. I think that if you''re getting lessons from Leroy you are a quick study and that he is a good teacher. Keep up the great work and I hope you do well with this and any other challenges you enter. All the best  MAX!', '2008-03-05 22:47:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(4542138, 645708, 50695, '<td valign="top">the reason this works can''t be explained. it''s not simply that it mixes a scant few highlights with overbearing dark tones and hints of a gray world. That''s not enough. The beauty is in the rhythm of the mix, the ingredients and where you put them... the repeated pairings: two faces, two poles, the two facing triangles in the upper right, two bench supports in the lower right, two windows in the upper left. The picture is almost nothing. It peers through the brink of dark chaos.</td>', 'the reason this works can''t be explained. it''s not simply that it mixes a scant few highlights with overbearing dark tones and hints of a gray world. That''s not enough. The beauty is in the rhythm of the mix, the ingredients and where you put them... the repeated pairings: two faces, two poles, the two facing triangles in the upper right, two bench supports in the lower right, two windows in the upper left. The picture is almost nothing. It peers through the brink of dark chaos.', '2008-03-05 22:54:03.000000', NULL, 1),
