(4547207, 652451, 32997, '<td valign="top">I haven''t a friggin'' clue why this is here and others are at the top, is it fear that this is another Icelandic victor that stops voters from looking, I don''t know..but the foreground is lovely, the rock in center holds it all together and the truck adds to the sense of adventure...<br/>it is a solid shot, strange score...</td>', 'I haven''t a friggin'' clue why this is here and others are at the top, is it fear that this is another Icelandic victor that stops voters from looking, I don''t know..but the foreground is lovely, the rock in center holds it all together and the truck adds to the sense of adventure...it is a solid shot, strange score...', '2008-03-08 00:53:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547208, 653006, 68504, '<td valign="top">Quite delightful, real feel for the place and action.</td>', 'Quite delightful, real feel for the place and action.', '2008-03-08 00:54:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547209, 652130, 70514, '<td valign="top">Glad to see your instincts are spot on.  Very interesting and full of curiosity.</td>', 'Glad to see your instincts are spot on.  Very interesting and full of curiosity.', '2008-03-08 00:54:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547210, 653110, 23002, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by trevytrev:</b></div><hr/><i> Great capture, site to see for sure! I thought you hated the bald shots..lol!Congrats man on a nice finish and a great photo! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hahaha.  Well I this is a wild bird.  I am not a big fan of the shots of baldy''s that are just headshots of captive birds and then given a title like "freedom bird" and things like that.    A real, wild bird shot is something of a different feather so to speak. :)<br/> <br/>Not to say that headshots of captive birds cannot be beautiful, but they are not the same as the "real" thing.  No offense to those that take and enjoy those shots, it is just that if it is a captive bird, please say so in the title so that it is known that the shot was easier to get, and that the bird is certainly not a "freedom bird" when it cannot even fly free.<br/> <br/>A shot taken in a sanctuary where the birds can still come and go as they please, but are slightly tamer, are still wild to me because they have the ability to come and go as they please.  <br/> <br/>I just wonder when I see headshots if they are not showing the whole bird because of the tether attached to the poor thing.  Again, no offense to anyone if that is what you are into.</td>', 'Originally posted by trevytrev: Great capture, site to see for sure! I thought you hated the bald shots..lol!Congrats man on a nice finish and a great photo!   Hahaha.  Well I this is a wild bird.  I am not a big fan of the shots of baldy''s that are just headshots of captive birds and then given a title like "freedom bird" and things like that.    A real, wild bird shot is something of a different feather so to speak. :) Not to say that headshots of captive birds cannot be beautiful, but they are not the same as the "real" thing.  No offense to those that take and enjoy those shots, it is just that if it is a captive bird, please say so in the title so that it is known that the shot was easier to get, and that the bird is certainly not a "freedom bird" when it cannot even fly free. A shot taken in a sanctuary where the birds can still come and go as they please, but are slightly tamer, are still wild to me because they have the ability to come and go as they please.   I just wonder when I see headshots if they are not showing the whole bird because of the tether attached to the poor thing.  Again, no offense to anyone if that is what you are into.', '2008-03-08 00:54:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547211, 649939, 32997, '<td valign="top">nice symbolic start and great Fargo like background...solid work!</td>', 'nice symbolic start and great Fargo like background...solid work!', '2008-03-08 00:54:52.000000', NULL, 0),
