(4547637, 641407, 51793, '<td valign="top">Well let me say that you defiantly have your own style of editing. please please please make sure that you read the rules carefully and don''t get busted doing this in basic editing.  Oh yeah and welcome to the site. You are going to do very well here and should ribbon in no time at all. Watch the text... 99.9% of the time text can not be added to pictures. I know you didn''t do it here but I have see people add text and not know so I''m just warning ya. <br/> <br/>Can''t wait to see what other images you can produce. <br/> <br/>Joe<br/></td>', 'Well let me say that you defiantly have your own style of editing. please please please make sure that you read the rules carefully and don''t get busted doing this in basic editing.  Oh yeah and welcome to the site. You are going to do very well here and should ribbon in no time at all. Watch the text... 99.9% of the time text can not be added to pictures. I know you didn''t do it here but I have see people add text and not know so I''m just warning ya.  Can''t wait to see what other images you can produce.  Joe', '2008-03-08 07:04:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547653, 650398, 85886, '<td valign="top">The HDR effect it a bit too strong - there''s haloing happening all around the plant, and there are unsightly hard shadows cast onto the wall behind.  The vase itself isn''t that interesting or appealing, and the wall paper seems a very muted colour.  The flowers themselves could do with some sharpness and richer colour palette.  And compositionally a vase of flowers just isn''t that interesting.  Hope this helps.</td>', 'The HDR effect it a bit too strong - there''s haloing happening all around the plant, and there are unsightly hard shadows cast onto the wall behind.  The vase itself isn''t that interesting or appealing, and the wall paper seems a very muted colour.  The flowers themselves could do with some sharpness and richer colour palette.  And compositionally a vase of flowers just isn''t that interesting.  Hope this helps.', '2008-03-08 07:09:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547676, 652576, 39850, '<td valign="top">In response to your request for feedback - My first thoughts are that this is blurry and perhaps too much contrast.  There is visible noise from pp.  Those are the biggest detractors in this image in my opinion, however you may have done those things intentionally, if so, it is difficult to offer an opinion or suggestions, as only you know what it is you are aiming to create.  If not intentional, then I think more detail discernible in the ''stick in the mud'', so that the viewer can see what it is (hard to tell from this silhouette).  I like that the horizon appears straight but again, the position you have placed it in the frame may be intentional, as may be the position / angle that you placed the ''stick'' in / over the water.  There appears to be some foreign elements in the fore, which if garbage is not appealing, but could be shells.  The highlights are extreme too, including the sky - but again I wonder if this was intentional.  Having said that, overall it is quite a dark image (including feel) with no real focal point and not abstract enough to give interest. All my opinion of course.  I didn''t get to this while voting, but likely wouldn''t have scored it very high.</td>', 'In response to your request for feedback - My first thoughts are that this is blurry and perhaps too much contrast.  There is visible noise from pp.  Those are the biggest detractors in this image in my opinion, however you may have done those things intentionally, if so, it is difficult to offer an opinion or suggestions, as only you know what it is you are aiming to create.  If not intentional, then I think more detail discernible in the ''stick in the mud'', so that the viewer can see what it is (hard to tell from this silhouette).  I like that the horizon appears straight but again, the position you have placed it in the frame may be intentional, as may be the position / angle that you placed the ''stick'' in / over the water.  There appears to be some foreign elements in the fore, which if garbage is not appealing, but could be shells.  The highlights are extreme too, including the sky - but again I wonder if this was intentional.  Having said that, overall it is quite a dark image (including feel) with no real focal point and not abstract enough to give interest. All my opinion of course.  I didn''t get to this while voting, but likely wouldn''t have scored it very high.', '2008-03-08 07:20:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547682, 652888, 39850, '<td valign="top">Thank you for continuing to share these.  This has beautiful colors.  Not sure on the frame, wonder about selecting one of the colors within, rather than the green you have chosen.  I also wonder about a variation in composition to allow this nebula to dominate the frame more.  I couldn''t help but notice the ''shafts'' of the star cropped out on the right - perhaps including that (if it wouldn''t detract from the .. err, ''star'' of the show), or else eliminating those blue elements, may have made this an even stronger image.  Of course, I cannot comment on the ''astrotechnicals'' - maybe ''one day''.</td>', 'Thank you for continuing to share these.  This has beautiful colors.  Not sure on the frame, wonder about selecting one of the colors within, rather than the green you have chosen.  I also wonder about a variation in composition to allow this nebula to dominate the frame more.  I couldn''t help but notice the ''shafts'' of the star cropped out on the right - perhaps including that (if it wouldn''t detract from the .. err, ''star'' of the show), or else eliminating those blue elements, may have made this an even stronger image.  Of course, I cannot comment on the ''astrotechnicals'' - maybe ''one day''.', '2008-03-08 07:25:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547686, 651764, 85886, '<td valign="top">Good job Andi - grats on the decent score and top 20.  FWIW there''s some entries up there above you that I''m surprised scored as highly as they did in a FS.  Where did you shoot this?</td>', 'Good job Andi - grats on the decent score and top 20.  FWIW there''s some entries up there above you that I''m surprised scored as highly as they did in a FS.  Where did you shoot this?', '2008-03-08 07:27:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547689, 649537, 39850, '<td valign="top">Came back to add to my somewhat ''short'' comment below (but hopefully my score spoke some too).  I liked this, especially the concept - wondered during voting about a tighter crop at the bottom to eliminate the oof area of the paw, and reduce the strong highlights which just take a little too much away from those ''pure'' looking whiskers.</td>', 'Came back to add to my somewhat ''short'' comment below (but hopefully my score spoke some too).  I liked this, especially the concept - wondered during voting about a tighter crop at the bottom to eliminate the oof area of the paw, and reduce the strong highlights which just take a little too much away from those ''pure'' looking whiskers.', '2008-03-08 07:29:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547705, 653110, 70661, '<td valign="top">Awesome! Congrats on a great capture and score!!</td>', 'Awesome! Congrats on a great capture and score!!', '2008-03-08 07:35:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547713, 645384, 70661, '<td valign="top">I love this Jelena. Very touching!</td>', 'I love this Jelena. Very touching!', '2008-03-08 07:44:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547719, 643900, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8.  Really liked it and was a second away from commenting but didn''t.  Really liked the curvature of the terrain and the colors of the brush / flora.  Nice image. <i>edit: refined</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-08 14:56:26.</i></td>', 'I gave this an 8.  Really liked it and was a second away from commenting but didn''t.  Really liked the curvature of the terrain and the colors of the brush / flora.  Nice image. edit: refined', '2008-03-08 07:48:56.000000', '2008-03-08 14:56:26.000000', 0),
(4547726, 652576, 88010, '<td valign="top">The girder is a silouette and has no detail. Fill flash would have fixed that without blowing out the background. Way too much noise, evidenced by all the color dots in the sand. The sky is a bit burned and a graduated neutral density filter could have brought some detail to the sky and left the sand properly exposed. And in general it doesn''t look "tack sharp" which makes me wonder if you used a tripod or hand held.<br/> <br/>I didn''t even look through the open challenge, but you asked for constructive criticism and i hope my thoughts help. Remember, we each see thigns a bit differently and thus shoot them a bit differently. What is right for me might not be for you. My own posts are not the greatest. But the fun for me was meeting specific challenges which pushed me to shoot things I normally would not. Thus increasing my own depth of knowledge in this great hobby.<br/> <br/>Good luck.<br/> <br/>Ward</td>', 'The girder is a silouette and has no detail. Fill flash would have fixed that without blowing out the background. Way too much noise, evidenced by all the color dots in the sand. The sky is a bit burned and a graduated neutral density filter could have brought some detail to the sky and left the sand properly exposed. And in general it doesn''t look "tack sharp" which makes me wonder if you used a tripod or hand held. I didn''t even look through the open challenge, but you asked for constructive criticism and i hope my thoughts help. Remember, we each see thigns a bit differently and thus shoot them a bit differently. What is right for me might not be for you. My own posts are not the greatest. But the fun for me was meeting specific challenges which pushed me to shoot things I normally would not. Thus increasing my own depth of knowledge in this great hobby. Good luck. Ward', '2008-03-08 07:52:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547727, 653018, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 7.  Liked the colors, including the background which complemented the bird.  Difficult at this angle, but to be able to see a little more of the eye, likely make this a stronger image in my opinion.</td>', 'I gave this a 7.  Liked the colors, including the background which complemented the bird.  Difficult at this angle, but to be able to see a little more of the eye, likely make this a stronger image in my opinion.', '2008-03-08 07:52:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547729, 652929, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 7.  Liked the perspective and unusual coupling of the mosque and pews/tables.  The lights were/are nice.</td>', 'I gave this a 7.  Liked the perspective and unusual coupling of the mosque and pews/tables.  The lights were/are nice.', '2008-03-08 07:53:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547734, 653082, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6.  Liked the tone/b&amp;w - works very well.  A more refined/tighter crop on the left and at the bottom would likely have made this a much stronger image in my opinion, that coupled with 720, especially in a Challenge like this.</td>', 'I gave this a 6.  Liked the tone/b&w - works very well.  A more refined/tighter crop on the left and at the bottom would likely have made this a much stronger image in my opinion, that coupled with 720, especially in a Challenge like this.', '2008-03-08 07:55:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547736, 652576, 88010, '<td valign="top">Oh, one other thing I should have added. The horizon should "almost" never cross the center of a pic. That said, spome rules get broken for good reason. But in this case I think the centered horizon is a mistake. Use the horizon as a tool to bring impotrance to either the sky or earth. In this shot had the horizon been higher leaving the sky only 1/3 of the scene it would have put more importance on the foreground and the stick. Which seemed to be what you were trying to convey.  If the sky has a lot of nice clouds and points of interest then do the opposite and allow it to hold 2/3 of the scene, but know that is whee the viewers eye will go. There are of course exceptions to this rule too. <br/> <br/>Enjoy the hobby.</td>', 'Oh, one other thing I should have added. The horizon should "almost" never cross the center of a pic. That said, spome rules get broken for good reason. But in this case I think the centered horizon is a mistake. Use the horizon as a tool to bring impotrance to either the sky or earth. In this shot had the horizon been higher leaving the sky only 1/3 of the scene it would have put more importance on the foreground and the stick. Which seemed to be what you were trying to convey.  If the sky has a lot of nice clouds and points of interest then do the opposite and allow it to hold 2/3 of the scene, but know that is whee the viewers eye will go. There are of course exceptions to this rule too.  Enjoy the hobby.', '2008-03-08 07:57:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547740, 645384, 63269, '<td valign="top">The LIGHTING is jaw-dropping. The way it falls on the subjects face, so delicately, and with that touch of gold... incredible work. Very well done! :)</td>', 'The LIGHTING is jaw-dropping. The way it falls on the subjects face, so delicately, and with that touch of gold... incredible work. Very well done! :)', '2008-03-08 08:00:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547741, 652976, 39850, '<td valign="top">No expert on night photography, but this appears to be overexposed.  Especially with the new rules, perhaps trying to combine differently exposed images to create more even lighting may improve upon what it seems you are aspiring to.  The reflection is nice.</td>', 'No expert on night photography, but this appears to be overexposed.  Especially with the new rules, perhaps trying to combine differently exposed images to create more even lighting may improve upon what it seems you are aspiring to.  The reflection is nice.', '2008-03-08 08:00:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547742, 649120, 39850, '<td valign="top">Perhaps a more extreme crop and composition may have produced a stronger (and true) abstract, as is, this doesn''t appear as an abstract image, despite your title.  The colors overall and flare on the lights in the trees are nice.</td>', 'Perhaps a more extreme crop and composition may have produced a stronger (and true) abstract, as is, this doesn''t appear as an abstract image, despite your title.  The colors overall and flare on the lights in the trees are nice.', '2008-03-08 08:01:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547744, 653115, 8891, '<td valign="top">Ken this is simply gorgeous. Big congrats on your Red and New PB!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-08 21:23:53.</i></td>', 'Ken this is simply gorgeous. Big congrats on your Red and New PB!', '2008-03-08 08:02:07.000000', '2008-03-08 21:23:53.000000', 0),
(4547746, 648966, 39850, '<td valign="top">I nearly commented on this during the Challenge, but didn''t, mainly due to time.  I like the concept but the two biggest detractors were the overblown color (yellow) and the lack of sharp focus in the fore area.  A variation in composition as well to balance this out would likely have helped as well.  I don''t know much about shooting with extension tubes, but I think that the focal area is very narrow, if I''m not mistaken, so you would need to adjust your angle/subject to compensate for that.</td>', 'I nearly commented on this during the Challenge, but didn''t, mainly due to time.  I like the concept but the two biggest detractors were the overblown color (yellow) and the lack of sharp focus in the fore area.  A variation in composition as well to balance this out would likely have helped as well.  I don''t know much about shooting with extension tubes, but I think that the focal area is very narrow, if I''m not mistaken, so you would need to adjust your angle/subject to compensate for that.', '2008-03-08 08:04:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547748, 652724, 39850, '<td valign="top">I recall this from voting and thought perhaps you were going for a stock type image.  If so, I think concentrating on a ''cleaner'', smoother and brighter overall finish would have helped an image such as this.</td>', 'I recall this from voting and thought perhaps you were going for a stock type image.  If so, I think concentrating on a ''cleaner'', smoother and brighter overall finish would have helped an image such as this.', '2008-03-08 08:05:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547750, 646341, 39850, '<td valign="top">The detail at the top is good, including that of the sky - I think this picture suffered mainly due to lack of context / the crop.</td>', 'The detail at the top is good, including that of the sky - I think this picture suffered mainly due to lack of context / the crop.', '2008-03-08 08:06:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547751, 652942, 39850, '<td valign="top">Depending on the control over the foreground lighting, perhaps a longer exposure to bring the background into play may have helped this image.</td>', 'Depending on the control over the foreground lighting, perhaps a longer exposure to bring the background into play may have helped this image.', '2008-03-08 08:07:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547753, 644433, 39850, '<td valign="top">Perhaps the background elements competed too much for the main subject in this image, and lost viewers attention - including my own during voting - I was one of your 5s.</td>', 'Perhaps the background elements competed too much for the main subject in this image, and lost viewers attention - including my own during voting - I was one of your 5s.', '2008-03-08 08:08:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547759, 651777, 39850, '<td valign="top">Beautiful scene and colors.  Like the long exposure effect.  Compositionally seems ''out'' though, perhaps it is the horizontal framing, not sure.  I didn''t get to this while voting, hypothetically - probably around a 6. <i>edit:wording</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-08 08:29:48.</i></td>', 'Beautiful scene and colors.  Like the long exposure effect.  Compositionally seems ''out'' though, perhaps it is the horizontal framing, not sure.  I didn''t get to this while voting, hypothetically - probably around a 6. edit:wording', '2008-03-08 08:13:05.000000', '2008-03-08 08:29:48.000000', 0),
(4547761, 649515, 76335, '<td valign="top">Nice perspective and DOF. I like the earthy tones also. Lots of things to look for and pick out of this one. It looks like an early morning shot (am I right?). Not sure what I think of the border, but I say that about most borders. Nice job!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-08 08:14:51.</i></td>', 'Nice perspective and DOF. I like the earthy tones also. Lots of things to look for and pick out of this one. It looks like an early morning shot (am I right?). Not sure what I think of the border, but I say that about most borders. Nice job!', '2008-03-08 08:14:35.000000', '2008-03-08 08:14:51.000000', 0),
(4547764, 650063, 39850, '<td valign="top">Beautiful ceiling and your focus seems very good.  Colors are well captured.  Symmetry-wise, this seems a touch out, maybe a nudge up on the left - but difficult to nail this type of image.</td>', 'Beautiful ceiling and your focus seems very good.  Colors are well captured.  Symmetry-wise, this seems a touch out, maybe a nudge up on the left - but difficult to nail this type of image.', '2008-03-08 08:16:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547765, 651764, 68586, '<td valign="top">Andi - the eye looks a little crazy - but apart from that , quite magnificent.<br/> <br/>Good shot - good result.</td>', 'Andi - the eye looks a little crazy - but apart from that , quite magnificent. Good shot - good result.', '2008-03-08 08:16:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547766, 653110, 68586, '<td valign="top">Great shot - love his look of concentration  :- )</td>', 'Great shot - love his look of concentration  :- )', '2008-03-08 08:18:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547769, 649537, 76335, '<td valign="top">Nice sharp focus, and black-and-white was an excellent choice. The cropping seems a little tight on the right; I might have gotten just a bit more of the nose or face to orient the viewer. But it''s a minor point. Well done! <br/></td>', 'Nice sharp focus, and black-and-white was an excellent choice. The cropping seems a little tight on the right; I might have gotten just a bit more of the nose or face to orient the viewer. But it''s a minor point. Well done! ', '2008-03-08 08:19:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547770, 652800, 68586, '<td valign="top">A very nice shot and one that would look great as a poster or canvas print.<br/> <br/></td>', 'A very nice shot and one that would look great as a poster or canvas print. ', '2008-03-08 08:20:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547773, 652543, 88523, '<td valign="top">Strong strong image...indeed.</td>', 'Strong strong image...indeed.', '2008-03-08 08:22:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547774, 647408, 76335, '<td valign="top">Very nice! I like how it reveals itself slowly -- there are a lot of subtle textures other things here. Some voters may have missed that.</td>', 'Very nice! I like how it reveals itself slowly -- there are a lot of subtle textures other things here. Some voters may have missed that.', '2008-03-08 08:23:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547777, 641531, 39850, '<td valign="top">Beautiful scene - one that I imagine stops you in your tracks.  The landscape alone without the clouds is very nice, I can''t discern much detail in the fore at this size, so .. difficult.  I wonder whether the clouds cropped to eliminate the top left darker one may have given this image a little extra.  A very strong crop of the clouds to allow the land to shine through more would also make a good image, but .. a different one.</td>', 'Beautiful scene - one that I imagine stops you in your tracks.  The landscape alone without the clouds is very nice, I can''t discern much detail in the fore at this size, so .. difficult.  I wonder whether the clouds cropped to eliminate the top left darker one may have given this image a little extra.  A very strong crop of the clouds to allow the land to shine through more would also make a good image, but .. a different one.', '2008-03-08 08:26:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547779, 653117, 76335, '<td valign="top">Nicely composed and a great candid shot. I like the geometry (the white grid in the building was the very first thing to catch my eye). The colors seem to "bleed" a little bit, and the focus isn''t quite what it should be; my temptation would have been to do this in black-and-white. Nice job overall, though.</td>', 'Nicely composed and a great candid shot. I like the geometry (the white grid in the building was the very first thing to catch my eye). The colors seem to "bleed" a little bit, and the focus isn''t quite what it should be; my temptation would have been to do this in black-and-white. Nice job overall, though.', '2008-03-08 08:28:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547781, 650475, 55838, '<td valign="top">You always seem to milk those good scores out of me don''tcha?!  Fun shot and I''m glad to have such a nice neighbor at the finish line!</td>', 'You always seem to milk those good scores out of me don''tcha?!  Fun shot and I''m glad to have such a nice neighbor at the finish line!', '2008-03-08 08:29:45.000000', NULL, 0),
