(4551704, 652799, 656, '<td valign="top">Looking at this I can''t help but be reminded about the advice I read from Steve McCurry, in this <a href="//www.pdn-pix.com/pdn/features/article_display.jsp?vnu_content_id=1003701105" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">interview with him.</a> <br/> <br/><i>When asked what those two years of travel taught him, McCurry says simply, Just because someones wearing a turban, doesnt mean its an interesting photo."</i> <br/> <br/>I know I have the same issue - I see something cool and take a very literal image of it, rather than working to find an interesting photo of something interesting.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Looking at this I can''t help but be reminded about the advice I read from Steve McCurry, in this interview with him.  When asked what those two years of travel taught him, McCurry says simply, Just because someones wearing a turban, doesnt mean its an interesting photo."  I know I have the same issue - I see something cool and take a very literal image of it, rather than working to find an interesting photo of something interesting. ', '2008-03-10 09:24:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4551714, 650495, 67723, '<td valign="top">Wow it seems like the commenters weren''t all that busy in this challenge.  (including me :(    This is a great shot!  I especially like the misty look above the rocks.</td>', 'Wow it seems like the commenters weren''t all that busy in this challenge.  (including me :(    This is a great shot!  I especially like the misty look above the rocks.', '2008-03-10 09:26:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4551931, 653014, 67723, '<td valign="top">Technically this is good but it could have been made much better by getting down closer to the perspective of the duck.  With this "I''m human and looking down on you" perspective there is no communication between the bird and the viewer.  The way it is, is just kind of a so-so shot.  Doesn''t really hold your interest at all.</td>', 'Technically this is good but it could have been made much better by getting down closer to the perspective of the duck.  With this "I''m human and looking down on you" perspective there is no communication between the bird and the viewer.  The way it is, is just kind of a so-so shot.  Doesn''t really hold your interest at all.', '2008-03-10 09:57:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4551934, 650067, 67723, '<td valign="top">In my opinion this was seriously underrated.!!!</td>', 'In my opinion this was seriously underrated.!!!', '2008-03-10 09:58:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4552037, 645292, 46853, '<td valign="top">Virkilega flott hjá þér.</td>', 'Virkilega flott hjá þér.', '2008-03-10 10:50:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4552192, 652799, 63269, '<td valign="top">I got zero comments during a challenge once with this:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=583201" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/737/120/583201.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/737/120/583201.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/737/120/583201.jpg"/></a>. <br/>Frustrating, isn''t it? :) <br/>Here''s my two cents on your photo. If I had been voting I admit I probably would not have been moved to make a comment on this either. There''s nothing necessarily <i>wrong </i>with the image, but nothing outstanding either. The quality certainly ranks higher than "snapshot" thanks to the duotone colors and the nice shallow DOF, but it''s not very interesting. Perhaps getting closer to the subject and making the shallow DOF more dramatic might help out. Maybe a different, more dynamic composition would also increase the impact - the two people on the right don''t really add much to the shot... Also a personal nit-pic for me is the specific shade of color you chose to make this - it''s sort of greenish blueish, and not very pleasant in my opinion. Perhaps a warmer brown color might have worked better? <br/> <br/>Hope this was helpful! :) I think this has potential... the subject has captivating eyes.</td>', 'I got zero comments during a challenge once with this:. Frustrating, isn''t it? :) Here''s my two cents on your photo. If I had been voting I admit I probably would not have been moved to make a comment on this either. There''s nothing necessarily wrong with the image, but nothing outstanding either. The quality certainly ranks higher than "snapshot" thanks to the duotone colors and the nice shallow DOF, but it''s not very interesting. Perhaps getting closer to the subject and making the shallow DOF more dramatic might help out. Maybe a different, more dynamic composition would also increase the impact - the two people on the right don''t really add much to the shot... Also a personal nit-pic for me is the specific shade of color you chose to make this - it''s sort of greenish blueish, and not very pleasant in my opinion. Perhaps a warmer brown color might have worked better?  Hope this was helpful! :) I think this has potential... the subject has captivating eyes.', '2008-03-10 12:21:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4552340, 649887, 80058, '<td valign="top">What a lovely shot!</td>', 'What a lovely shot!', '2008-03-10 13:23:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4552381, 652848, 15648, '<td valign="top">LOVE Hurrel. i learned about lighting from his Hollywood Portrait book. <br/> <br/>Nice job on this</td>', 'LOVE Hurrel. i learned about lighting from his Hollywood Portrait book.  Nice job on this', '2008-03-10 13:46:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4552399, 652297, 50695, '<td valign="top">I like the grainy effect.</td>', 'I like the grainy effect.', '2008-03-10 13:54:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4552406, 652965, 50695, '<td valign="top">This photo is now being used as an example of how limited the definition of "technical merit" is. This photo would not exist without the "technical" decisions you made.<br/> <br/>Yet some people claim that the "technicals" are not good on this photo. I might have to use this as a litmus test for my new Photography He-Man Club...</td>', 'This photo is now being used as an example of how limited the definition of "technical merit" is. This photo would not exist without the "technical" decisions you made. Yet some people claim that the "technicals" are not good on this photo. I might have to use this as a litmus test for my new Photography He-Man Club...', '2008-03-10 13:58:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4552620, 645960, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very cool shot. The color is fantastic.</td>', 'Very cool shot. The color is fantastic.', '2008-03-10 15:44:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4552648, 650398, 23484, '<td valign="top">Nice Terry, I think you did a great job with the processing. This shot would look cool with one of those actions that I sent.</td>', 'Nice Terry, I think you did a great job with the processing. This shot would look cool with one of those actions that I sent.', '2008-03-10 15:53:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4552719, 649537, 52336, '<td valign="top">I think this merely suffered from "free study glut", whereby the subtler entries get drowned out by the candy-esque ones in a challenge with many entrants.  My opinion is that this is a delicately subtle and a gentle, understated take on a pet portrait.  It may have been even more effective had the nose also been in focus, perhaps helping to anchor the delicacy of the whiskers.  That focus field is right at his chin and whiskers, and though a tad nit-picky, this fact detracts slightly for me.  Overall a very lovely photo.  I adore cats.</td>', 'I think this merely suffered from "free study glut", whereby the subtler entries get drowned out by the candy-esque ones in a challenge with many entrants.  My opinion is that this is a delicately subtle and a gentle, understated take on a pet portrait.  It may have been even more effective had the nose also been in focus, perhaps helping to anchor the delicacy of the whiskers.  That focus field is right at his chin and whiskers, and though a tad nit-picky, this fact detracts slightly for me.  Overall a very lovely photo.  I adore cats.', '2008-03-10 16:11:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4552863, 649537, 35334, '<td valign="top">Tell Thomas I think he has great whiskers; they are certainly better than mine.<br/> <br/>I really liked this. It is not "yet another cat picture." It features the whiskers and says something about how important they are to a cat. My whiskers don''t do much useful for me except catch stray bits of spaghetti sauce, but his are an important part of his sensory system and they help him interact with things in close quarters.<br/> <br/>The paw. What is that paw doing there? Is it a distraction that draws attention away from the whiskers? Or does it contribute to the feeling that he is interacting with something in close quarters? I haven''t decided about this.<br/> <br/>--DanW<br/></td>', 'Tell Thomas I think he has great whiskers; they are certainly better than mine. I really liked this. It is not "yet another cat picture." It features the whiskers and says something about how important they are to a cat. My whiskers don''t do much useful for me except catch stray bits of spaghetti sauce, but his are an important part of his sensory system and they help him interact with things in close quarters. The paw. What is that paw doing there? Is it a distraction that draws attention away from the whiskers? Or does it contribute to the feeling that he is interacting with something in close quarters? I haven''t decided about this. --DanW', '2008-03-10 16:45:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4552919, 648777, 89426, '<td valign="top">I havn''t seen this before. This is an awesome photograph. Very nice job.</td>', 'I havn''t seen this before. This is an awesome photograph. Very nice job.', '2008-03-10 17:22:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4553003, 649537, 34113, '<td valign="top">You are the master of otherworldly whiskers. They add an extra dimension that transcends catdom.</td>', 'You are the master of otherworldly whiskers. They add an extra dimension that transcends catdom.', '2008-03-10 18:10:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4553071, 649537, 83313, '<td valign="top">It does not wow me any, but it is a nice and detailed shot of the cat''s whiskers. One of those shots that is really pretty good, but just does not bowl me over or grab me. I''ll say I would have probably sixed it, but in voting it could have gotten a five from me, not really sure.<br/><u> <br/>Edited to add:</u> I don''t like to read others comments before I add my own, as I don''t want them to influence what I say. I think Louis may have nailed it down better than I did. In a free study, you have a glut of "wow" shots that people have worked on all month, or saved their best for, and the subtle but good ones get lost in the crowd.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-10 18:55:56.</i></td>', 'It does not wow me any, but it is a nice and detailed shot of the cat''s whiskers. One of those shots that is really pretty good, but just does not bowl me over or grab me. I''ll say I would have probably sixed it, but in voting it could have gotten a five from me, not really sure. Edited to add: I don''t like to read others comments before I add my own, as I don''t want them to influence what I say. I think Louis may have nailed it down better than I did. In a free study, you have a glut of "wow" shots that people have worked on all month, or saved their best for, and the subtle but good ones get lost in the crowd.', '2008-03-10 18:52:45.000000', '2008-03-10 18:55:56.000000', 0),
(4553109, 650231, 83313, '<td valign="top">Feedback per your post in the forums:<br/>A very cool scene. My initial impression was that both the background and foreground are so awesome that my attention is divided. Perhaps zooming in a little more to show the details on the peak would have been a good shot as well.</td>', 'Feedback per your post in the forums:A very cool scene. My initial impression was that both the background and foreground are so awesome that my attention is divided. Perhaps zooming in a little more to show the details on the peak would have been a good shot as well.', '2008-03-10 19:04:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554019, 650340, 19982, '<td valign="top">I like the composition.  Good work on the exposure!  Maybe just a little more contrast to make it pop more.  <br/></td>', 'I like the composition.  Good work on the exposure!  Maybe just a little more contrast to make it pop more.  ', '2008-03-11 00:49:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554064, 652219, 53814, '<td valign="top">leaves me asking more questions than it answered. great.</td>', 'leaves me asking more questions than it answered. great.', '2008-03-11 01:16:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554295, 652799, 47852, '<td valign="top">As Haneck mentioned, the biggest problem for me with this shot is the coloring you''ve chosen.  I think this color scheme is difficult to pull off with a shot of people.  A true b/w or a duotone with a warmer color would have worked better for me.  Besides that, it''s a nice shot, but doesn''t evoke an emotion, make me wonder about the people or tell a story.  The men appear to have no interaction, and there isn''t any particular emotion shown.  By flipping through a few of your other shots from this trip, I think there are several others that might have been a better choice, especially considering this was a free study and you didn''t need to worry about DNMC comments.  Hope that helps some.</td>', 'As Haneck mentioned, the biggest problem for me with this shot is the coloring you''ve chosen.  I think this color scheme is difficult to pull off with a shot of people.  A true b/w or a duotone with a warmer color would have worked better for me.  Besides that, it''s a nice shot, but doesn''t evoke an emotion, make me wonder about the people or tell a story.  The men appear to have no interaction, and there isn''t any particular emotion shown.  By flipping through a few of your other shots from this trip, I think there are several others that might have been a better choice, especially considering this was a free study and you didn''t need to worry about DNMC comments.  Hope that helps some.', '2008-03-11 06:26:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554475, 652894, 56744, '<td valign="top">Another breathtaking image. All my life I only saw borealis in photographs, but the most amazing ones came from you, Mr Iceland.</td>', 'Another breathtaking image. All my life I only saw borealis in photographs, but the most amazing ones came from you, Mr Iceland.', '2008-03-11 08:34:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554675, 652574, 89723, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments both during the challenge and after. Even you Toddhead! I was pleasantly surprised by my score. I was really limited by my surroundings on this shot. I don''t have a flash yet and the lighting in this gymnasium isn''t that great, but I did the best I could. Look forward to future challenges.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments both during the challenge and after. Even you Toddhead! I was pleasantly surprised by my score. I was really limited by my surroundings on this shot. I don''t have a flash yet and the lighting in this gymnasium isn''t that great, but I did the best I could. Look forward to future challenges.', '2008-03-11 10:29:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554762, 652693, 60862, '<td valign="top">Ha!  Was he already holding the sign? Their expressions are terrific.</td>', 'Ha!  Was he already holding the sign? Their expressions are terrific.', '2008-03-11 11:21:42.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(4554893, 650231, 67697, '<td valign="top">What happens for me, when I look at this photo, is that my attention is divided between the foreground and the background.  I see an almost pretty painterly effect in the background and then the foreground seems somewhat unnatural to me.  But it''s cool tho because it looks like melting butter or carmel.  I think it would have scored higher if the voter can tell what you really want the focal point of the picture to be.</td>', 'What happens for me, when I look at this photo, is that my attention is divided between the foreground and the background.  I see an almost pretty painterly effect in the background and then the foreground seems somewhat unnatural to me.  But it''s cool tho because it looks like melting butter or carmel.  I think it would have scored higher if the voter can tell what you really want the focal point of the picture to be.', '2008-03-11 12:20:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555001, 650231, 30982, '<td valign="top">I had no problem discerning what it was and sharing your enjoyment of the stark contrast in colors.  This could be very subjective (ha!) because I happen to really like rocks and formations and stuff.  Your other commenters have provided potential reasons why it didn''t score higher.  It is a pretty cool shot, though.</td>', 'I had no problem discerning what it was and sharing your enjoyment of the stark contrast in colors.  This could be very subjective (ha!) because I happen to really like rocks and formations and stuff.  Your other commenters have provided potential reasons why it didn''t score higher.  It is a pretty cool shot, though.', '2008-03-11 13:11:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555006, 653138, 30982, '<td valign="top">Got an 8 from me - very well done.</td>', 'Got an 8 from me - very well done.', '2008-03-11 13:12:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555013, 650340, 30982, '<td valign="top">Great energy to this - I very much like their poses and the looks you captured.  This looks like it was probably a very fun shoot!</td>', 'Great energy to this - I very much like their poses and the looks you captured.  This looks like it was probably a very fun shoot!', '2008-03-11 13:14:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555026, 650340, 16241, '<td valign="top">awesome.</td>', 'awesome.', '2008-03-11 13:18:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555052, 648508, 73235, '<td valign="top">I just realized I had not checked on your picture. <br/>Congratulations to the new PB. It certainly has the attributes of a classical painting.</td>', 'I just realized I had not checked on your picture. Congratulations to the new PB. It certainly has the attributes of a classical painting.', '2008-03-11 13:27:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555066, 652593, 91095, '<td valign="top">Over all a nice shot. A few observations:<br/> <br/>- A 3/4 pose of the subject would be better with side lighting.<br/>- Elevated angle shooting down at subject would have been more flattering (no double chin)<br/>- The triple bordering detracts from the purpose of the image.<br/>- The title does not match the action/activity of the subject. "Thoughtful" would be more fitting.</td>', 'Over all a nice shot. A few observations: - A 3/4 pose of the subject would be better with side lighting.- Elevated angle shooting down at subject would have been more flattering (no double chin)- The triple bordering detracts from the purpose of the image.- The title does not match the action/activity of the subject. "Thoughtful" would be more fitting.', '2008-03-11 13:39:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555080, 652006, 29011, '<td valign="top">What a great location. Think you captured the awe of the place, and as usual I''m sure it''s even better in person.</td>', 'What a great location. Think you captured the awe of the place, and as usual I''m sure it''s even better in person.', '2008-03-11 13:45:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555132, 653119, 87808, '<td valign="top">I have the exact same light fixture, in fact about 3of them around the house.  I wonder if we hadthe same house builder!!!</td>', 'I have the exact same light fixture, in fact about 3of them around the house.  I wonder if we hadthe same house builder!!!', '2008-03-11 14:09:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555245, 653119, 19708, '<td valign="top">I don''t have a foyer.<br/>Nor a light like that.<br/>But I did stay at a Holiday Inn Express.<br/> <br/>:)</td>', 'I don''t have a foyer.Nor a light like that.But I did stay at a Holiday Inn Express. :)', '2008-03-11 15:17:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555252, 652799, 91095, '<td valign="top">I like this shot a lot. Its very photojournalistic in nature. Not at all touristie.<br/> <br/>The composition is very good. The sharpness and depth of field is on the money. The subject is not playing to the camera. I even like the slightly green (ektachrome) tint, it gives it a dated feel, much like an older Life magazine image.<br/> <br/>It would also be very compelling with an extreme crop of just the subject himself.</td>', 'I like this shot a lot. Its very photojournalistic in nature. Not at all touristie. The composition is very good. The sharpness and depth of field is on the money. The subject is not playing to the camera. I even like the slightly green (ektachrome) tint, it gives it a dated feel, much like an older Life magazine image. It would also be very compelling with an extreme crop of just the subject himself.', '2008-03-11 15:20:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555337, 653109, 50695, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 7. The juxtaposition is wild. The two types of windmills just don''t want to be near each other!</td>', 'I gave this a 7. The juxtaposition is wild. The two types of windmills just don''t want to be near each other!', '2008-03-11 16:08:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555341, 652474, 50695, '<td valign="top">wow, under a 5. Sorry, you got underrated for this shot. I gave you a 7.</td>', 'wow, under a 5. Sorry, you got underrated for this shot. I gave you a 7.', '2008-03-11 16:11:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555344, 653113, 50695, '<td valign="top">I dig it. I gave it a 7.</td>', 'I dig it. I gave it a 7.', '2008-03-11 16:11:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555378, 647945, 57060, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for their comments, very much appeciated. I''ve been out of the country for the last two weeks and really didn''t know how this one would do. I really liked the simplicity and honesty of it - and of course the subject ;-)<br/> <br/>Jack</td>', 'Thanks to all for their comments, very much appeciated. I''ve been out of the country for the last two weeks and really didn''t know how this one would do. I really liked the simplicity and honesty of it - and of course the subject ;-) Jack', '2008-03-11 16:27:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555663, 649340, 90658, '<td valign="top">I thought that this was too "noisy."  A sharper focus OR brighter lighting, not both.  Good attempt, though.</td>', 'I thought that this was too "noisy."  A sharper focus OR brighter lighting, not both.  Good attempt, though.', '2008-03-11 18:10:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555707, 652978, 52130, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hotpasta:</b></div><hr/><i> I really like the eyes, but the pose doesn''t flatter her...she is stunning, but a more relaxed pose would have done her justice... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>0.o? I was relaxed...just chillin'' in my car...but I kinda see what you mean :) i do look a bit strained.</td>', 'Originally posted by hotpasta: I really like the eyes, but the pose doesn''t flatter her...she is stunning, but a more relaxed pose would have done her justice...   0.o? I was relaxed...just chillin'' in my car...but I kinda see what you mean :) i do look a bit strained.', '2008-03-11 18:37:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555953, 641578, 90495, '<td valign="top">This is so nicely captured. The dof is spot on and the colours are magnificent. The bg may be just a bit busy but the sharpness of the bee commands your attention. GJ. I need to get myself a long macro lens.</td>', 'This is so nicely captured. The dof is spot on and the colours are magnificent. The bg may be just a bit busy but the sharpness of the bee commands your attention. GJ. I need to get myself a long macro lens.', '2008-03-11 19:59:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4556064, 651752, 2553, '<td valign="top">Honestly, this is one of the finest portraits I''ve ever seen; reading your story brought tears to my eyes.  Your work is superb.</td>', 'Honestly, this is one of the finest portraits I''ve ever seen; reading your story brought tears to my eyes.  Your work is superb.', '2008-03-11 20:44:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4556472, 649556, 4793, '<td valign="top">Congratulations/abeautiful shot</td>', 'Congratulations/abeautiful shot', '2008-03-11 23:46:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4556507, 650475, 62318, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the score. What a very comical scene.</td>', 'Congrats on the score. What a very comical scene.', '2008-03-12 00:03:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4556514, 641531, 57620, '<td valign="top">For me the frosted trees are the strongest part of the image the clouds are good but man the trees behind the cows have great light and structure. I would have voted that image a 7 or 8 while giving your posted image a 6. <br/> <br/></td>', 'For me the frosted trees are the strongest part of the image the clouds are good but man the trees behind the cows have great light and structure. I would have voted that image a 7 or 8 while giving your posted image a 6.  ', '2008-03-12 00:05:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4556994, 653115, 30807, '<td valign="top">My word - what a lovely shot! It manages to look extremely cold with the blue bits, but warm and cosy with the sunrise, especially on the water, and I think the glow or softening filtering adds to the warm feel. I suspect I would have warmed the blue, so it all looked warm, but that would have spoiled it, probably. Well deserved ribbon!</td>', 'My word - what a lovely shot! It manages to look extremely cold with the blue bits, but warm and cosy with the sunrise, especially on the water, and I think the glow or softening filtering adds to the warm feel. I suspect I would have warmed the blue, so it all looked warm, but that would have spoiled it, probably. Well deserved ribbon!', '2008-03-12 03:30:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557014, 652814, 82763, '<td valign="top">Awesome!</td>', 'Awesome!', '2008-03-12 03:51:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557020, 652872, 39110, '<td valign="top">Glad this worked out well :)</td>', 'Glad this worked out well :)', '2008-03-12 03:57:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557062, 652857, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is excellent - very nice work.</td>', 'This is excellent - very nice work.', '2008-03-12 04:45:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557147, 648777, 8643, '<td valign="top">This is immaculate - so well done!<br/>Congratulations on a superb job - inspirational.</td>', 'This is immaculate - so well done!Congratulations on a superb job - inspirational.', '2008-03-12 06:33:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557543, 652731, 2764, '<td valign="top">This is absolutely beautiful.  I am so glad I stumbled on it!  It''s an image that will stay with me for years and years.</td>', 'This is absolutely beautiful.  I am so glad I stumbled on it!  It''s an image that will stay with me for years and years.', '2008-03-12 09:29:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557769, 652993, 67697, '<td valign="top">So cool that the shadow from the windows reflects on the woman and then you see the windows in the background as well.  I love her look and this moment makes me wonder what he is about to say (or has already said).  Very cool photo.</td>', 'So cool that the shadow from the windows reflects on the woman and then you see the windows in the background as well.  I love her look and this moment makes me wonder what he is about to say (or has already said).  Very cool photo.', '2008-03-12 10:51:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557777, 652565, 67697, '<td valign="top">I love how you filled the frame with that beautiful hair!  I love all the waves and curls.  This is a very sweet photo.</td>', 'I love how you filled the frame with that beautiful hair!  I love all the waves and curls.  This is a very sweet photo.', '2008-03-12 10:54:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557835, 652130, 68947, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot, Michelle!  I feel that the red sign really just adds to this shot.  A new front page addition shot for your profile portfolio!  Poor little guy......let him out once in awhile, will ya?! *grin*<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-12 22:19:20.</i></td>', 'Wonderful shot, Michelle!  I feel that the red sign really just adds to this shot.  A new front page addition shot for your profile portfolio!  Poor little guy......let him out once in awhile, will ya?! *grin*', '2008-03-12 11:06:43.000000', '2008-03-12 22:19:20.000000', 0),
(4558650, 652800, 63269, '<td valign="top">The colors are absolutely luscious. I love it!</td>', 'The colors are absolutely luscious. I love it!', '2008-03-12 16:12:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4558807, 652800, 67723, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote in this challenge but I like this photo more than some of the photos that scored higher.  I don''t know about your other photos as much but to me this one and still life in general has a very hard time ribboning in a free study, as good as it may be.  It seems to me like landscape/sky/and a few portraits make it to the top in free studies consistently.  As far as still life goes this is as good as it gets and 19th place out of 455 proves that.  For those that rated below 5.5 and didn''t leave feedback is mostly likely because there is nothing technically wrong with the photo, but simply that they don''t "dig" this kind of photo.  Don''t lose heart, your one of my favorite photographers on here because of your style (esp. the muted colors!)  Keep it up!</td>', 'I didn''t vote in this challenge but I like this photo more than some of the photos that scored higher.  I don''t know about your other photos as much but to me this one and still life in general has a very hard time ribboning in a free study, as good as it may be.  It seems to me like landscape/sky/and a few portraits make it to the top in free studies consistently.  As far as still life goes this is as good as it gets and 19th place out of 455 proves that.  For those that rated below 5.5 and didn''t leave feedback is mostly likely because there is nothing technically wrong with the photo, but simply that they don''t "dig" this kind of photo.  Don''t lose heart, your one of my favorite photographers on here because of your style (esp. the muted colors!)  Keep it up!', '2008-03-12 16:57:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4558984, 652313, 45706, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>The composition is really nice. It is framed well but could use a little tweaking with the crop. Following the rule of thirds (which can be broken--I know), I would scoot the windmill over to the left, and allow a tad more room at the top. These are minor issues comparatively. <br/> <br/>Focus and DOF are good.<br/> <br/>The biggest problem with this photo is the exposure. Most users, as I have found it, like to see nice even histograms with vivid color. The contents in this photo seems to be good candidates for these elements. I know the environment (setting of sun, or rising; I can''t tell) may not be easy to accomplish this and fight the underexposure. <br/> <br/>Also, the streak right next to the windmill blade is a little distracting as it seems out of place.<br/> <br/>The big picture: I think you were on the right track with this photo, but with the challenging environment yielding some technical errors this photo performed mediocre in the challenge.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work though, do not get discouraged. Keep shooting!<br/> <br/>Disclaimer: The above content is the opinion of one man who probably couldn''t do any better himself. The views expressed here do not represent the views of DPChallenge, its affiliates or subsidiaries.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! The composition is really nice. It is framed well but could use a little tweaking with the crop. Following the rule of thirds (which can be broken--I know), I would scoot the windmill over to the left, and allow a tad more room at the top. These are minor issues comparatively.  Focus and DOF are good. The biggest problem with this photo is the exposure. Most users, as I have found it, like to see nice even histograms with vivid color. The contents in this photo seems to be good candidates for these elements. I know the environment (setting of sun, or rising; I can''t tell) may not be easy to accomplish this and fight the underexposure.  Also, the streak right next to the windmill blade is a little distracting as it seems out of place. The big picture: I think you were on the right track with this photo, but with the challenging environment yielding some technical errors this photo performed mediocre in the challenge. Keep up the good work though, do not get discouraged. Keep shooting! Disclaimer: The above content is the opinion of one man who probably couldn''t do any better himself. The views expressed here do not represent the views of DPChallenge, its affiliates or subsidiaries.', '2008-03-12 17:46:00.000000', NULL, 0),
